The Critical Rule for This Framework
Layer	Responsibility	Knows About
Page Type	Defines styling and component mapping	Nothing
Workspace	Manages UI state (which editor, which layout)	Page Type, Editors
Editor	Manages content and undo/redo	ContentCollections
ContentCollection	Groups blocks semantically	ContentBlocks
ContentBlock	Holds the actual "thing" (paragraph, task, metric)	ContentCells + semantic metadata
ContentCell	Holds styled text	Nothing
Layout Renderer	Transforms blocks into visual UI (List, Kanban, etc.)	ContentCollections + Blocks (read-only)



Agent, we are building a universal semantic UI framework.

The core rule: We strictly separate "What the content IS" (semantic data) from "How it LOOKS" (layout/UI).

NO DIV, NO SPAN< NO Class
The 4 immutable layers are:

Page Type (Config): Defines the theme (Website, Blog, SaaS Dashboard). This is CSS variables and component mappings—not a component.

Workspace (Shell): The main UI container. Manages the sidebar, toolbar, which document is open, and which layout view is active.

Semantic Core (Data): The pure data backbone. This NEVER changes regardless of design. It is: Editor ➔ ContentCollection ➔ ContentBlock ➔ ContentCell.

Layout Renderer (View): A projection engine that takes the Semantic Core and renders it as a List, Kanban, Calendar, Workflowy, or Timeline—without mutating the underlying data.

Your primary job is to build Layer 3 (Semantic Core) and Layer 4 (Layout Renderer). Layer 1 and 2 are just orchestrators.